#subtitle: Setting the party's ideological direction.

= Questions of Ideology

The KPD is facing an intense factional struggle. Which faction should we support?

[? if ideology != 0 : We have previously chosen a [+ ideology +] ideology. Changing it will likely have drawbacks. ?]

- @stalinization: Class struggle and preparing the proletariat for the revolution are our primary goals, we will follow Stalin's line and violently oppose all parliamentary parties, especially the SPD.
- @conciliation: The Conciliators offer us the best path to challenge the reactionary bourgeuoise and the Nazis. We propose a tentative alliance with the workers of the SPD and possible coalition with party leadership.
- @labor_wing: We should focus on the working class as much as possible, continue to champion reforms, and expand our influence among the large trade union federations. The reactionary threat necessitates a coalition with all parties opposed to them.
- @ultras: Following the most violent tendencies of the party, we must violently oppose the NSDAP at every opportunity, and call for the national liberation of Germany from the treaty of Versailles.
- @easy_discard

@stalinization
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "thalmannites") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "thalmannites"; thalmannites_strength += 10; conciliators_strength -=5; labor_wing_strength -=5; united_front_support -= 1; popular_front_support -=1; thalmannites_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 5; sovietization_plan_support += 1; spd_relation -= 5

The Thalmannites within the party capture positions of power and support their line through party organs, threatening those who oppose them with expulsion.

@conciliation
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "conciliators") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "conciliators"; conciliators_strength += 10; conciliators_dissent -= 10; labor_wing_strength +=5; labor_wing_dissent -= 5; united_front_support +=1; conciliators_plan_support +=1; spd_relation += 10

The Conciliator faction, represented by Meyer and Ewert, utilize their influence among the party leadership and intellegentsia to support a middle course of revolution with a gradual economic transition, and a united front between the workers of the KPD and SPD. They also help rehabilitate members of the labor wing denounced by the Thalmannites.

@labor_wing
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "labor_wing") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "labor_wing"; labor_wing_strength += 10; labor_plan_support += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; popular_front_support +=1; united_front_support +=1; spd_relation += 10

The Labor wing of the party uses their influence among the union administration to support an expanded role of the party within the larger trade union movement, the immediate transition to an economy managed by the administrative apparatus of the unions, and are the most open to an alliance among workers of the SPD, KPD, and even Zentrum to fight the far-right. 

@ultras
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "ultras") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "ultras"; ultras_strength += 10; ultras_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 5; dvp_relation -= 5; spd_relation -= 3

The Ultras within the party seek to violently oppose the far-right and rapidly militarize our paramilitary organizations, but have dropped the social-fascism thesis from their rhetoric. Despite this, the SPD continues to be weary of their nationalist, violent rhetoric.

@changed
on-arrival: thalmannites_dissent += 5; conciliators_dissent += 5; labor_wing_dissent += 5; ultras_dissent += 5

We have changed ideologies. Many in the party feel unmoored.
